\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab To establish a baseline, identify gaps, and calculate indicative performance.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Before developing the CIP and before verification.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Periodically when practices or farm circumstances change.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 1.\tab Complete the General Questions worksheet.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 2.\tab Answer all applicable questions in the SAQ worksheet.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 3.\tab Read requirements and guidance before answering Yes or Not Applicable.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 4.\tab Keep evidence for each Yes response.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 5.\tab Review the Performance worksheet and use identified gaps in improvement planning.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Important:\b0  Completing the SAQ alone does not authorize a verified Bronze, Silver, or Gold claim.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.3 FSA 3.0 Training Toolkit\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 fsa-3.0-training-toolkit.pdf\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Visual, farmer-friendly explanations corresponding to the FSA questions.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Examples of required practices, records, training, evidence, decisions, and controls.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Practical guidance across land rights, farm management, inputs, soil, water, biodiversity, labour, safety, and other assessment topics.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab During farmer onboarding and workshops.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Before or while completing the SAQ.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When a farmer needs help understanding a question or evidence expectation.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When developing training or corrective/improvement activities.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Locate the slide matching the SAQ question.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Review its examples with the farmer.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Compare expectations with actual farm practices and records.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Record gaps for action, but confirm formal requirements in the SAQ and Implementation Framework.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.4 FSA Continuous Improvement Module V3.0\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 fsa-continuous-improvement-module-v3.0-eng.docx\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Guidance for developing and implementing a CIP.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Farmer-engagement and outreach guidance.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab A CIP template and a progress-report template.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab A flexible five-step process: identify priorities; establish targets; develop activities; confirm timeline and accountability; monitor and adjust.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab After priority screening and self-assessment.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Before verification when documenting the required improvement approach.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab During annual progress review and re-verification preparation.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Engage farmers and stakeholders in selecting priorities.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Define a baseline, target, due date, activities, and responsible people for each priority.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Monitor progress, record lessons, and adjust the plan when needed.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Maintain internal progress reports at least annually.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.5 FSA Outcome Measurement Handbook V3.1\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 fsa-outcome-measurement-handbook-v-3.1_september2023.pdf\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Guidance on why, when, and how to measure outcomes.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Criteria for choosing an appropriate measurement tool.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Detailed sections on greenhouse gases and climate, soil, biodiversity, and water.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Example calculator tools, including Cool Farm Tool, Fieldprint Platform, and Puma Platform.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When moving from practice assessment to measuring actual results.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When selecting a calculator, metric, sampling approach, or baseline method.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When evaluating whether CIP activities produce intended outcomes.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 1.\tab Define the outcome, purpose, audience, and measurement scale.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 2.\tab Review the relevant outcome chapter.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 3.\tab Compare tools for scientific robustness, relevance, data needs, cost, transparency, and outputs.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 4.\tab Establish and consistently repeat the measurement method.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 5.\tab Feed results back into the CIP.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.6 FSA Benchmarking Protocol V3.01\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 fsa_benchmarking-protocol-v-3.01.pdf\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab The process for comparing certifications, company programs, legislation, national schemes, and diagnostic tools against FSA.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Assessment of scheme content, governance, and assurance.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Application, consultant review, results, claims, validity, fees, and governance requirements.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Key distinction\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab \b FSA Aligned:\b0  Content has been benchmarked and governance requirements are met, but FSA minimum verification requirements are not met. FSA-equivalent volume claims are not allowed.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab \b FSA Equivalent:\b0  Content, governance, and assurance requirements are met. Equivalent-volume claims may be supported within the approved benchmark scope.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When an existing scheme may replace some or all direct FSA implementation.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When a scheme owner seeks formal recognition.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When interpreting aligned versus equivalent status or planning a benchmark.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Check existing Benchmarking Results first.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Define the exact standard version, country, product, legislation combination, and intended claim.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Follow the application process and use an approved benchmarking consultant.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.7 FSA Benchmarking Results \u8212? December 12, 2025\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 fsa-benchmarking-results-12-12-25.xlsx\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab FSA 3.0 and historical FSA 2.1 benchmark results.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Expired results and equivalence-level explanations.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Scheme name, version, benchmark date, scheme type, combinations, geography, product, claim type, question coverage, and performance level.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Before requiring farms to duplicate FSA assessment activities.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Before commissioning a benchmark.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When validating an FSA aligned/equivalent claim and its scope.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Match the exact scheme version, country/region, product, and required combinations.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Confirm whether the result is Aligned or Equivalent and whether it is Bronze, Silver, Gold, Not Yet Bronze, or expired.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Do not assume that a result for one version, product, geography, or combination applies to another.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.8 FMG Verification Audit Annual Reporting Template\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 fsa-fmg-verification-audit-annual-reporting-template_1.0-1-1.docx\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab The required report on FMG membership and size after a Letter of Attestation is issued.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab FMG and Letter of Attestation details, farm counts, current farm list, FMG declaration, and Verification Body review.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Within four weeks of the first and second anniversaries of the Letter of Attestation validity start date.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Key thresholds\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab More than 10% turnover in FMG membership; or\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab More than a 10% increase in the total number of farms.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 If either threshold is exceeded, the Letter of Attestation is invalidated but retains validity for six months from the relevant anniversary to allow a new farm-performance audit. The management-system audit does not need to be repeated if completed within the previous three years.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Maintain a current farm register.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Compare current composition with the audited group.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Calculate turnover and growth, attach the current farm list, submit the report on time, and retain Verification Body confirmation.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 4.9 SAI Platform RTF\u8211?NIAB Database 2025\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b Repository file:\b0  \f1\cf2 sai-platforms-rtf-niab-database-2025.xlsx\f0\cf1 \par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b What it contains\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab A methodology, collated evidence table, glossary, and practice-specific evidence worksheets.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Evidence concerning practices such as reduced soil disturbance, controlled traffic, cover crops, mulching, intercropping, crop rotation, habitat protection, agroforestry, buffers, grazing, manure, nutrients, pest management, irrigation, feed, and herd/flock management.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b When to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When selecting evidence-supported regenerative-agriculture activities for a CIP.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab When reviewing likely links between practices and outcomes.\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 \b How to use it\b0 \par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Read the Introduction, Methodology, and CollatedTable worksheets first.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Review the worksheet for the practice being considered.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Use the evidence to inform decisions, not as a substitute for FSA assessment, verification, or outcome measurement.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa120\b\cf1\fs28 5. Responsibilities by Role\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 FMG Coordinator\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Use the Implementation Framework to establish and operate the management system.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Coordinate priority screening, SAQ sampling/completion, training, CIP development, verification, volume records, and annual reporting.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Maintain evidence, farm registers, progress reports, and communication with the Verification Body.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 Farmer or Farm Manager\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Complete the SAQ accurately and retain supporting records.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Participate in training, improvement planning, and outcome-data collection where applicable.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Inform the FMG Coordinator when practices or farm circumstances change.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 Buyer or Sustainability Manager\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Define the business purpose and required claims.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Check benchmarked schemes before requiring direct FSA implementation.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Support resources for improvement and outcome measurement.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Ensure external claims match verified or benchmarked scope.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 Scheme Owner\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Use the Benchmarking Protocol and Results to understand recognition options.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Maintain scheme governance, assurance, and current documentation.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Seek review when meaningful scheme changes could affect the benchmark result.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\cf2\fs24 Verification-Preparation Team\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Use the Implementation Framework as the primary requirements reference.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Verify that SAQ answers, management-system records, CIP evidence, farm lists, volume records, and claims are complete and consistent.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa120\b\cf1\fs28 6. Records to Maintain\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\sa120\fs21\cf1 A well-managed FSA program should maintain, as applicable:\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Defined program scope and objectives.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab FMG membership and farm register.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Roles, responsibilities, and coordinator appointment.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Priority screening outputs.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Completed SAQs and supporting evidence.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Training records.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab CIP and annual progress reports.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Outcome-measurement method, baseline, input data, and results.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Sampling records.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Volume-accounting records.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Verification reports and Letter of Attestation.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Year-one and year-two annual FMG reports and Verification Body confirmations.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Evidence supporting any benchmarked-scheme claim.\par
\pard\par
\pard\keepn\sb300\sa120\b\cf1\fs28 7. Common Mistakes to Avoid\b0\cf1\fs21\par
\pard\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Treating the Training Toolkit as a replacement for formal SAQ or Implementation Framework requirements.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Making a verified performance claim based only on a completed SAQ.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Using Not Applicable without checking whether it is permitted and keeping a justification.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Assuming a benchmark applies to a different standard version, geography, product, or legislation combination.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Confusing FSA Aligned with FSA Equivalent.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Using an equivalent claim outside the approved benchmark scope.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Creating a CIP without measurable targets, owners, deadlines, monitoring, or farmer engagement.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Changing outcome-measurement methods between baseline and follow-up without documenting the impact.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Missing the year-one or year-two FMG annual reporting deadlines.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\tx360\fs21\cf1 \bullet\tab Failing to monitor whether FMG turnover or growth exceeds 10%.\par
\pard\par
